{"outcome":"board","supportType":"FirstThenBoard","title":"Daughter's Dino Morning","theme":"Dinosaurs","sensorySupports":[],"sensorySupportOther":null,"cards":[{"sequenceNo":1,"role":"First","label":"Brush teeth","imagePrompt":"Flat vector icon, plain white background, no detail: a toothbrush with toothpaste","altText":"A toothbrush with a blob of toothpaste on it"},{"sequenceNo":2,"role":"Then","label":"Swing outside","imagePrompt":"Flat vector icon, plain white background, no detail: a playground swing","altText":"A playground swing hanging from a frame"}],"script":[{"phase":"Before","phrase":"Brush teeth first, then swing."},{"phase":"During","phrase":"Brush teeth now."},{"phase":"OnCompletion","phrase":"Teeth done. Now swing."},{"phase":"IfRefusal","phrase":"Brush first, then swing."}],"plan":{"placement":"Hang the board on the bathroom wall beside the sink, at your daughter's eye level, where she can see both cards before she starts.","boardAction":"When her teeth are finished, take the Brush teeth card off the board and point to the Swing outside card.","reinforcement":"As soon as the Brush teeth card is off, take her outside to swing that same minute.","ifChallengingBehavior":"Keep your focus on getting the brushing done, then move on to the swing as the board shows.","generalization":"Use the same two cards for bedtime teeth brushing, with another adult in the house.","promptHierarchy":[{"level":1,"kind":"VisualPoint","instruction":"Point to the Brush teeth card and say nothing else."},{"level":2,"kind":"Gesture","instruction":"Tap the Brush teeth card, then tap the toothbrush in her hand."},{"level":3,"kind":"Verbal","instruction":"Say 'Check the board.' Then point to the Brush teeth card."},{"level":4,"kind":"Model","instruction":"Brush your own teeth beside her at the sink while she does hers."},{"level":5,"kind":"PhysicalGuide","instruction":"Briefly guide her hand with the toothbrush to the first few teeth, then let go."}],"evidenceBasis":[{"practice":"Antecedent Package","technique":"cueing and prompting/prompt fading procedures"},{"practice":"Behavioral Package","technique":"reinforcement"}],"citations":["triad-visual-supports-p1-3.docx, chunk 12","triad-visual-supports-p1-3.docx, chunk 13","nsp-established-treatments-p11-19.docx, chunk 3","nsp-established-treatments-p11-19.docx, chunk 4"],"reasoning":"A First-Then board fits because the obstacle is one non-preferred task with a clear reward after it, and the swing is something she already likes to do. Swinging outside is the Then because the parent can deliver it within a minute, and it follows the brushing on the card so the sequence is what she learns."}
